Title: Select c-ares' pre-Vista fallbacks, leaving iphlpapi a plain static import
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

10 of node.exe's fatal static imports are iphlpapi entry points that arrived
with Vista. 8 of them are c-ares':

  NotifyIpInterfaceChange, CancelMibChangeNotify2   event/ares_event_configchg.c
  GetBestRoute2                                    ares_sysconfig_win.c
  GetUnicastIpAddressTable, FreeMibTable            ares_addrinfo_localhost.c
  ConvertInterfaceIndexToLuid,                      util/ares_iface_ips.c
    ConvertInterfaceLuidToNameA
  if_nametoindex, if_indextoname                   util/ares_iface_ips.c,
                                                   ares_getnameinfo.c

c-ares already supports a target without them -- every call site has an
#ifdef fallback for older toolchains -- so this is a configuration question,
not a porting one. The config-change watcher drops to RegNotifyChangeKeyValue
on the Tcpip and Tcpip6 Interfaces keys, ares_os_if_nametoindex and
ares_os_if_indextoname go through ares_iface_ips() (GetAdaptersAddresses),
the interface name comes from address->AdapterName, the route metric becomes
(ULONG)-1, and system loopback enumeration returns ARES_ENOTFOUND, which the
caller already handles by using the built-in loopback addresses.

The obvious lever is the wrong one. All six HAVE_ macros sit in one
_WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600 block in config-win32.h, so compiling c-ares at 0x0501
would clear them in a line -- and would also clear CARES_THREADS, gated on
the same test twenty lines up. Threading is wanted and already works: what it
needs is Vista synchronisation, which winwrap supplies, and that is precisely
what distinguishes it from the iphlpapi entry points, which winwrap does not.
So the gate here is CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI, named in that block and in
ares_addrinfo_localhost.c -- the one site gated on _WIN32_WINNT alone rather
than on a HAVE_ macro -- and defined in cares.gyp for the architectures this
tree builds for a pre-Vista Windows.

That leaves 2, both from libuv's uv_if_indextoname: ConvertInterfaceIndexToLuid
and ConvertInterfaceLuidToNameW. Those are winwrap's now -- src/net.cc, from
0.4.4 -- so the references are settled there and neither appears in node.exe's
iphlpapi imports. With all 10 accounted for, everything node.exe does import
from iphlpapi is something XP exports, and the DLL stays an ordinary static
import.

An earlier form of this patch delay-loaded iphlpapi instead, on the grounds
that node never calls uv_if_indextoname and so the thunk would never fire. It
left a residue: an addon that did call it faulted on XP, because a delay-load
failure raises rather than returns. Supplying the pair removes the residue and
the need for the delay-load with it, so the only change here to node.gypi is to
the comment patch 15 left, which said why iphlpapi was not in the delay-load
list and gave c-ares as the reason.

diff --git a/deps/cares/cares.gyp b/deps/cares/cares.gyp
index fee055c0..d8af547b 100644
--- a/deps/cares/cares.gyp
+++ b/deps/cares/cares.gyp
@@ -201,6 +201,17 @@
             '-lws2_32.lib',
             '-liphlpapi.lib'
           ],
+          'conditions': [
+            [ 'target_arch in "ia32 x64"', {
+              # These are the architectures this tree builds for a pre-Vista
+              # Windows -- XP for ia32, Server 2003 for x64 -- and c-ares is
+              # where 8 of node.exe's 10 pre-Vista iphlpapi imports come from.
+              # See src/lib/config-win32.h for what the define switches off
+              # and what each call site falls back to. A win-arm64 build has
+              # no legacy target to serve and keeps the Vista entry points.
+              'defines': [ 'CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI=1' ],
+            }],
+          ],
         }, {
           # Not Windows i.e. POSIX
           'cflags': [
diff --git a/deps/cares/src/lib/ares_addrinfo_localhost.c b/deps/cares/src/lib/ares_addrinfo_localhost.c
index cacd0237..2689caa1 100644
--- a/deps/cares/src/lib/ares_addrinfo_localhost.c
+++ b/deps/cares/src/lib/ares_addrinfo_localhost.c
@@ -147,8 +147,13 @@ static ares_status_t
   ares_system_loopback_addrs(int aftype, unsigned short port,
                              struct ares_addrinfo_node **nodes)
 {
+/* GetUnicastIpAddressTable and FreeMibTable are Vista, and unlike the rest of
+ * the iphlpapi uses they are gated on _WIN32_WINNT alone rather than on a
+ * HAVE_ macro -- so CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI has to be named here too. The
+ * #else returns ARES_ENOTFOUND, which is what the caller already handles by
+ * falling back to the built-in loopback addresses. */
 #if defined(USE_WINSOCK) && defined(_WIN32_WINNT) && _WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600 && \
-  !defined(__WATCOMC__)
+  !defined(__WATCOMC__) && !defined(CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI)
   PMIB_UNICASTIPADDRESS_TABLE table;
   unsigned int                i;
   ares_status_t               status = ARES_ENOTFOUND;
diff --git a/deps/cares/src/lib/config-win32.h b/deps/cares/src/lib/config-win32.h
index fc533c75..c28242bd 100644
--- a/deps/cares/src/lib/config-win32.h
+++ b/deps/cares/src/lib/config-win32.h
@@ -360,8 +360,18 @@
 /* Define to 1 if you have the `RegisterWaitForSingleObject' function. */
 #define HAVE_REGISTERWAITFORSINGLEOBJECT 1
 
+/* CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI is for a build whose target predates these, which
+   _WIN32_WINNT cannot express here: lowering that would take CARES_THREADS
+   above with it, and threading is wanted -- the Vista synchronisation it needs
+   is supplied by winwrap, whereas the iphlpapi entry points below are not.
+   Every use of these six has an #ifdef fallback: the config-change watcher
+   drops to RegNotifyChangeKeyValue on the Tcpip Interfaces keys,
+   ares_os_if_nametoindex and ares_os_if_indextoname go through
+   ares_iface_ips(), the interface name comes from address->AdapterName, and
+   the route metric becomes (ULONG)-1. */
 #if defined(_WIN32_WINNT) && (_WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600) && \
-  !defined(__WATCOMC__) && !defined(WATT32)
+  !defined(__WATCOMC__) && !defined(WATT32) &&           \
+  !defined(CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI)
 /* Define if you have if_nametoindex() */
 #  define HAVE_IF_NAMETOINDEX 1
 /* Define if you have if_indextoname() */
diff --git a/node.gypi b/node.gypi
--- a/node.gypi
+++ b/node.gypi
@@ -100,13 +100,20 @@
           # plus /DELAYLOAD:dbghelp.dll, which is why Electron's XP build
           # imports dbghelp lazily and starts where this did not.
           #
-          # Deliberately not iphlpapi, whose 10 pre-Vista imports would also
-          # go quiet here: c-ares calls GetBestRoute2, NotifyIpInterfaceChange
-          # and GetUnicastIpAddressTable while setting up a channel, so
-          # delaying them trades a clean failure at load for a crash the first
-          # time anything resolves a name. That one wants c-ares' own
-          # HAVE_GETBESTROUTE2 and friends turned off instead, which selects
-          # fallbacks it already carries.
+          # Not iphlpapi, which stays a static import and needs no help to be
+          # one. It had 10 pre-Vista imports. c-ares accounted for 8 -- it
+          # called GetBestRoute2, NotifyIpInterfaceChange and
+          # GetUnicastIpAddressTable to bring a channel up -- and
+          # CARES_NO_VISTA_IPHLPAPI in deps/cares/cares.gyp removes those by
+          # selecting fallbacks c-ares already carries. The other 2 are
+          # libuv's uv_if_indextoname, wanting ConvertInterfaceIndexToLuid and
+          # ConvertInterfaceLuidToNameW, and winwrap supplies both (its
+          # src/net.cc), so they never reach iphlpapi's import list at all.
+          # What node.exe still imports from iphlpapi, XP exports.
+          #
+          # Delay-loading it would have hidden the 10 rather than dealt with
+          # them: a clean failure at load traded for a crash on the first
+          # name resolution.
           'DelayLoadDLLs': [
             'dbghelp.dll',
             'shell32.dll',
